Status: UNTESTED. The dev LLVM build on the orb was stopped at step
1516/2958 before clang was built, so this diff has not been compiled.
It applies to mbrock/fil-c 2d9aa147f871 (branch filnix) and is also pushed
as mbrock/fil-c branch orb/toolchain-fixes (a2ed1cb67ad). Fetch that
branch, or `sed -n '/^From /,$p' this.patch | git am` in a fil-c checkout.

What is verified: both assertions reproduce with the pinned compiler
(Fil-C 0.685) using the reproducers below; the new filc/tests were written
against the run-tests manifest format but not run.

Reproducer 1 (asserts `F.hasFnAttribute(Attribute::ReturnsTwice)`):

    #include <setjmp.h>
    static jmp_buf jb;
    int run(void) { int r = setjmp(jb); if (r) return r; longjmp(jb, 3); }
    int main(void) { return run() != 3; }
    /* clang -O2 -fno-builtin */

Reproducer 2 (asserts `G.getLinkage() != GlobalValue::CommonLinkage` in
lockDownLinkage):

    int x;
    int main(void) { return x; }
    /* clang -O2 -fcommon, or declare x __attribute__((common)) */

Things to check when building it:
- markSetjmpsReturnTwice() runs at the top of run(), before
  lowerIndirectBr(); the earlier pipeline stages (inliner options in
  BackendUtil.cpp's early-simplification callback) still see setjmp
  without returns_twice under -fno-builtin.
- Common -> WeakAny happens in lockDownLinkage(), before the comdat and
  global-collection loops. A common symbol declared with different sizes
  in different units becomes "first definition wins" instead of "largest
  wins".

From a2ed1cb67ad27aa6cdd9561469954c84513317c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Brockman <mikael@brockman.se>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:55:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FilPizlonator: recognize setjmp by name; give common symbols
 weak linkage

- With -fno-builtin, clang does not mark setjmp returns_twice, and the
  pass asserted F.hasFnAttribute(Attribute::ReturnsTwice). Mark setjmp,
  _setjmp and sigsetjmp and their direct calls returns_twice before
  anything else runs, as GCC recognizes them by name.
- Common symbols (-fcommon, __attribute__((common))) asserted in
  lockDownLinkage. Give them weak linkage, which the linker merges the
  same way across translation units.

Tests: setjmpnobuiltin, setjmpnobuiltinO0, commonsym, commonsymfcommon,
commonsymfail.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0e2af-3777-75da-ae86-0eab7fccd7af
Co-authored-by: Mikael Brockman <mikael@brockman.se>
